  ('Nick Bogaty', 'Chief Revenue Officer', 'Vercel', 23462, 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/nbogaty', 'vercel_executive', 'Vercel leadership', 'Sumble people search (CXO)', '[{"title":"Chief Revenue Officer","start_date":"2026-01","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","employer":{"organization_id":23462,"name":"Vercel","slug":"vercel","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/vercel","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/50h2TXQzxsaa"}},{"title":"Vice President, Adobe Express, Enterprise","start_date":"2024-08","end_date":"2026-01","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"I run the enterprise business for Adobe Express. Express is used by companies around the world to easily create beautifully designed stand-out content. Join us, we''re hiring!","employer":{"organization_id":235,"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/adobe","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/UxYK9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Chief Revenue Officer","start_date":"2022-07","end_date":"2024-08","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"I ran sales and post-sales for Instabug, the leader in mobile app performance. Instabug is used by engineering and product teams to debug, collect user feedback and improve performance for mobile apps. Pinterest, Okta, Adobe, Southwest Airlines, Dream11, General Motors, T-Mobile and many others rely on Instabug. I joined Instabug immediately following its Series B fundraise from Accel and Insight to build an Enterprise GTM. That included recruiting and hiring a sales team, enablement, creation of artifacts like a first meeting deck and demo, identification and targeting of companies/personas, outbound pipeline generation cadence and excellence, forecasting, sales process structure, value-selling, establishing technical and business criteria for PoCs and budget justification. Built from the ground up. Enterprise Results (y/y): + 70% Sales Growth + 60% ARPA + 45 pts. NDR + 100% Pipeline Growth + 85% RepVue Score","employer":{"organization_id":87557,"name":"Instabug","slug":"instabug","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/luciq","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/BgmGR73rqxXe"}},{"title":"Chief Revenue & Customer Officer","start_date":"2020-08","end_date":"2022-07","location":"San Francisco","description":"I joined AppDynamics prior to our record $3.7bn acquisition by Cisco in March 2017. During my time at AppDynamics we scaled the business from $120m to $600m in Annual Recurring Revenue. After overhauling the services and customer success teams as Chief Customer Officer resulting in the increase of Net Dollar Retention by 15 pts, I took over as Chief Revenue Officer while retaining my post-sales duties. My sales and post-sales organization was on order of 1250 employees. As CRO, I increased ARR from $400m to $600m in 2 years while reducing expenses in a drive toward profitability.","employer":{"organization_id":11341,"name":"AppDynamics","slug":"appdynamics","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/appdynamics","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/yHkTUHCj8ANz"}},{"title":"Chief Customer Officer","start_date":"2019-08","end_date":"2020-08","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","employer":{"organization_id":11341,"name":"AppDynamics","slug":"appdynamics","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/appdynamics","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/yHkTUHCj8ANz"}},{"title":"Vice President, Services & Customer Success","start_date":"2016-10","end_date":"2019-08","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","employer":{"organization_id":11341,"name":"AppDynamics","slug":"appdynamics","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/appdynamics","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/yHkTUHCj8ANz"}},{"title":"General Manager, Digital Publishing","start_date":"2013-11","end_date":"2016-09","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"I was the GM and co-founder of Digital Publishing Suite (DPS) at Adobe. DPS was the largest home-grown product created at Adobe since Acrobat growing to $50m ARR in 3 years. DPS allowed graphic designers to create interactive publications for mobile devices. We launched the product with Wired Magazine on the day of Apple''s introduction of the iPad (launch video below). I ran product, marketing and sales for DPS including personally executing multi-million dollar contracts with Conde Nast, Time, Meredith Corp and others.","employer":{"organization_id":235,"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/adobe","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/UxYK9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Senior Director, Digital Publishing","start_date":"2012-12","end_date":"2013-11","location":"Greater New York City Area","employer":{"organization_id":235,"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/adobe","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/UxYK9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Director, Digital Publishing","start_date":"2010-12","end_date":"2012-12","location":"Greater New York City Area","employer":{"organization_id":235,"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/adobe","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/UxYK9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Senior Manager, Digital Publishing","start_date":"2007-09","end_date":"2010-12","location":"Greater New York City Area","description":"Joined Adobe to monetize their electronic book business under Adobe Digital Editions. Created Adobe Content Server 4 which was a digital rights management system for electronic books. Awarded patent (US8793193B2) on supporting technology.","employer":{"organization_id":235,"name":"Adobe","slug":"adobe","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/adobe","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/UxYK9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Executive Director","start_date":"2002-09","end_date":"2007-09","location":"Greater New York City Area","description":"I ran the International Digital Publishing Forum (IDPF) which was a standards organization that made the EPUB file format. EPUB is to electronic books what the MP3 file format is to digital music. It is used by the Amazon Kindle and Apple''s iBooks application. The EPUB file format is now maintained by the W3C.","employer":{"name":"International Digital Publishing Forum"}},{"title":"Chief Executive Officer","start_date":"1999-08","end_date":"2002-09","location":"Greater New York City Area","description":"Started this company which was a marketplace exchange for intellectual property rights.","employer":{"name":"rightsworld.com"}}]'::jsonb),
  ('Mitchell Hashimoto', 'Board Member', 'Vercel', 23462, 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/mitchellh', 'board_member', 'Vercel leadership', 'Sumble people search (Board Member); Vercel board announcement', '[{"title":"Co-Founder","start_date":"2026-05","description":"We are building the multiplexer for all work.","employer":{"name":"Superlogical","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/superlogical"}},{"title":"Board Member","start_date":"2026-03","employer":{"organization_id":23462,"name":"Vercel","slug":"vercel","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/vercel","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/50h2TXQzxsaa"}},{"title":"Founder and CTO","start_date":"2016-06","end_date":"2021-07","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"Founded HashiCorp and changed roles from CEO to CTO in 2016 until July 2021. During this time, HashiCorp grew to nearly 1,500 employees, product downloads grew to over 100 million downloads per year, and we launched numerous new products. By the end of my tenure as CTO, we had over 1,700 enterprise customers including nearly 30% of the Fortune 500.","employer":{"organization_id":1586,"name":"HashiCorp","slug":"hashicorp","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/hashicorp","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/Uv0K9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Founder","start_date":"2012-11","end_date":"2023-12","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"Founded HashiCorp and changed roles from CTO to an individual contributor in 2021. HashiCorp makes a set of tools that are downloaded millions of times every month: Vagrant, Packer, Consul, Terraform, Vault, Nomad, Waypoint, and Boundary. These tools are used almost universally by tech companies worldwide and span multiple professional categories from developers to operators/IT as well as InfoSec.","employer":{"organization_id":1586,"name":"HashiCorp","slug":"hashicorp","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/hashicorp","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/Uv0K9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Founder and CEO","start_date":"2012-11","end_date":"2016-06","location":"San Francisco Bay Area","description":"Founded HashiCorp with Armon Dadgar and operated as CEO for almost four years, participating in every role along the way. During this time, HashiCorp grew from one employee to over 40, one open source tool to eight, zero dollars in revenue to seven figures in annually recurring revenue.","employer":{"organization_id":1586,"name":"HashiCorp","slug":"hashicorp","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/hashicorp","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/Uv0K9qdND2O"}},{"title":"Operations Engineer","start_date":"2010-10","end_date":"2012-11","location":"San Francisco, CA","description":"Designed and built the automation and tooling around infrastructure management from the ground up. In charge of monitoring, scalability, and reliability of the overall website. The tools built were built around Puppet, Python, Ruby, and Bash. Scaled from 1QPS at 200msec median response to 2000QPS at 20msec median response, processing over 100MM+ API requests per day.","employer":{"organization_id":109295,"name":"Kiip","slug":"kiip","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/kiip","sumble_url":"https://sumble.com/l/org/k2DgHL9w1JTj"}},{"title":"Developer","start_date":"2008-03","end_date":"2011-03","description":"Web developer which worked with many startups at various stages. I helped plan the architecture to scale sites from inception to having millions of active users. Specialized in Ruby-based web development, flash development, and frontend Javascript work.","employer":{"name":"CitrusByte","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/citrusbyte"}}]'::jsonb),
